She recalled coaching Drake as he punched in his Spanish lyrics line-by-line, along with making sure he nailed the pronunciation of words like &#8220;rico.&#8221; &#8220;I tried to just play a little bit with his pronunciation,&#8221; the 35-year-old added. &#8220;It was so much fun; he&#8217;s amazing.&#8221;

&#8220;Ahí&#8221; landed on Karol G&#8217;s No Me Arrepiento de Sentir Tanto album in August. The track peaked at No. 44 on the Billboard Hot 100 and topped the Hot Latin Songs chart, while La Bichota&#8217;s LP hit the Billboard 200&#8217;s top 10 (No. 8 peak).

Drake previously practiced his Spanish on songs like Romeo Santos&#8217; &#8220;Odio,&#8221; Bad Bunny&#8217;s &#8220;MIA,&#8221; For All the Dogs&#8217; &#8220;Gently&#8221; with Bad Bunny, as well as Chino Pacas and Fuerza Regida&#8217;s &#8220;Modo Capone&#8221; and $ome $exy $ongs 4 U &#8216;s &#8220;MEET YOUR PADRE.&#8221;

The 6 God pulled up to the Toronto stop of Karol G&#8217;s Viajando Por El Mundo Tropitour and then joined the Colombian superstar on stage at her Houston show, where they performed the live debut of &#8220;Ahí.&#8221; Drizzy also stuck around to perform &#8220;Janice STFU&#8221; and &#8220;One Dance.&#8221;

